/-!
# Consequences of a regular alteration of a local Noetherian domain

Let `(A, 𝔪)` be a Noetherian local domain and suppose that `Spec A` admits an alteration
`f : X ⟶ Spec A` with `X` regular. Then

1. `A` is regular after inverting one nonzero element;
2. the integral closure `B` of `A` in its fraction field is a finite `A`-module;
3. the completion of `B` along the ideal generated by `𝔪` is a normal ring;
4. the generic formal fibre `Aˆ ⊗_A Frac(A)` of `A` is regular.

Part (1) is [Stacks, Tag 0BGG] applied at the generic point: the dense regular open it produces
contains a nonempty basic open `D(a)`, whose ring of sections is `A_a`.

For part (2) put `C = Γ(X, 𝒪_X)`. Properness of `f` makes `C` a finite `A`-module, regularity of
`X` makes it an integrally closed domain, and dominance of `f` makes `A → C` injective; the
integral closure `B` of `A` in `Frac(A)` therefore maps injectively into `C` and is a submodule
of a finite module over the Noetherian ring `A`.

Part (3) is [Stacks, Tag 0BGH] for `B ⊆ C`: it reduces normality of `Bˆ` to normality of `Cˆ`.
Base change along the flat morphism `Spec Aˆ ⟶ Spec A` keeps `X` regular by
[Stacks, Tag 0BG6], hence normal, and the global sections of a quasi-compact normal scheme are a
normal ring because such a scheme is a finite coproduct of normal integral schemes
([Stacks, Tag 0357]). Flat base change in degree zero ([Stacks, Tag 02KH]) identifies those
global sections with `Aˆ ⊗_A C`, which `ofTensorProductAlgEquiv` identifies with `Cˆ`.

For part (4) choose an affine open `U ⊆ X` containing the generic point and put `R = Γ(X, U)`.
The base change `Spec (R ⊗_A Aˆ)` is an open subscheme of the regular scheme
`X ×_{Spec A} Spec Aˆ`, so `Aˆ ⊗_A R` is a regular ring; inverting `A ∖ {0}` and descending
along the faithfully flat `Frac(A)`-algebra `Frac(A) ⊗_A R` gives regularity of `Aˆ ⊗_A Frac(A)`.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.exists_isRegularRing_localizationAway_of_regular_alteration` — part (1).
* `AlgebraicGeometry.module_finite_integralClosure_of_regular_alteration` — part (2).
* `AlgebraicGeometry.isNormalRing_adicCompletion_integralClosure_of_regular_alteration` —
  part (3).
* `AlgebraicGeometry.isRegularRing_genericFormalFibre_of_regular_alteration` — part (4).

## Implementation notes

The integral closure of the source is `integralClosure A (FractionRing A)`, and the completion of
part (3) is taken along `(IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A).map (algebraMap A _)`, matching the shape in
which [Stacks, Tag 0BGH] is stated. Normality of a ring is `IsNormalRing`, the prime-by-prime
form of [Stacks, Tag 00GV]. The generic formal fibre is `AdicCompletion 𝔪 A ⊗[A] FractionRing A`:
that tensor product is the localization of `Aˆ` at the image of `A ∖ {0}`, which is the ring of
the fibre of `Spec Aˆ ⟶ Spec A` over the generic point.

**All four parts are unconditional and all four carry the tag attribute**, each naming the part
it proves. Parts (2) and (3) go through
`AlgebraicGeometry.FiniteGlobalSectionsOfProper`, the degree-zero case of [Stacks, Tag 02O6] for
the structure sheaf; that proposition is proved by
`AlgebraicGeometry.finiteGlobalSectionsOfProper` in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/ProperFiniteness/GlobalSectionsFinite.lean`, from the
hypothesis-free [Stacks, Tag 02O5] and [Stacks, Tag 02O6] of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/ProperCoherenceWitness/ChowStalk.lean`. The scheme-level form of
part (2) — finiteness of the normalization, the first assertion of [Stacks, Tag 0BGG] — is
`AlgebraicGeometry.normalization_isFinite_of_regular_alteration` in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/ResolutionOfSurfaces/ImpliedProperties/FiniteNormalization.lean`,
and is unconditional for the same reason.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BGI](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BGI)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BGG](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BGG)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BGH](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BGH)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BG6](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BG6)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02KH](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02KH)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02O6](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02O6)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0357](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0357)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits TopologicalSpace
open scoped TensorProduct nonZeroDivisors

universe u

/-! ### Ring-theoretic preliminaries -/

/-- The integral closure of a domain `A` in a fraction field `K` maps into any integrally closed
domain `C` which is integral over `A`: an element of `K` integral over `A` becomes, in the
fraction field of `C`, an element integral over `C`, hence an element of `C`. -/
def integralClosureToIntegrallyClosed
    {A C K : Type*} [CommRing A] [IsDomain A] [Field K] [Algebra A K] [IsFractionRing A K]
    [CommRing C] [Algebra A C] [Algebra.IsIntegral A C] [IsDomain C] [IsIntegrallyClosed C]
    (hAC : Function.Injective (algebraMap A C)) :
    integralClosure A K →ₐ[A] C :=
  have hAFrac : Function.Injective (algebraMap A (FractionRing C)) :=
    (IsFractionRing.injective C (FractionRing C)).comp hAC
  let fK : K →ₐ[A] FractionRing C :=
    { toRingHom := IsFractionRing.lift hAFrac
      commutes' := fun a => IsFractionRing.lift_algebraMap hAFrac a }
  let B := integralClosure A K
  letI : Algebra B (FractionRing C) := (fK.toRingHom.comp (B.val : B →+* K)).toAlgebra
  haveI : IsScalarTower A B (FractionRing C) :=
    IsScalarTower.of_algebraMap_eq' (by
      ext a
      exact (fK.commutes a).symm)
  IsIntegralClosure.lift A C (FractionRing C)

/-- The map of `integralClosureToIntegrallyClosed` is injective, both sides sitting inside the
fraction field of `C`. -/
theorem integralClosureToIntegrallyClosed_injective
    {A C K : Type*} [CommRing A] [IsDomain A] [Field K] [Algebra A K] [IsFractionRing A K]
    [CommRing C] [Algebra A C] [Algebra.IsIntegral A C] [IsDomain C] [IsIntegrallyClosed C]
    (hAC : Function.Injective (algebraMap A C)) :
    Function.Injective (integralClosureToIntegrallyClosed (K := K) hAC) := by
  have hAFrac : Function.Injective (algebraMap A (FractionRing C)) :=
    (IsFractionRing.injective C (FractionRing C)).comp hAC
  let fK : K →ₐ[A] FractionRing C :=
    { toRingHom := IsFractionRing.lift hAFrac
      commutes' := fun a => IsFractionRing.lift_algebraMap hAFrac a }
  let B := integralClosure A K
  let : Algebra B (FractionRing C) := (fK.toRingHom.comp (B.val : B →+* K)).toAlgebra
  have : IsScalarTower A B (FractionRing C) :=
    IsScalarTower.of_algebraMap_eq' (by
      ext a
      exact (fK.commutes a).symm)
  intro x y hxy
  refine Subtype.ext (fK.injective ?_)
  have hx : algebraMap C (FractionRing C)
      (integralClosureToIntegrallyClosed hAC x) = fK x.1 :=
    IsIntegralClosure.algebraMap_lift A C (FractionRing C) x
  have hy : algebraMap C (FractionRing C)
      (integralClosureToIntegrallyClosed hAC y) = fK y.1 :=
    IsIntegralClosure.algebraMap_lift A C (FractionRing C) y
  exact hx.symm.trans ((congrArg (algebraMap C (FractionRing C)) hxy).trans hy)

/-- If `A → R` is injective and `A` is a domain, then `K ⊗[A] R` is nonzero for `K` a fraction
field of `A`: that tensor product is a localization of `R` at the image of `A ∖ {0}`, and no
nonzero element of `A` maps to `0`. -/
theorem nontrivial_tensorProduct_fractionRing
    {A R K : Type*} [CommRing A] [IsDomain A] [CommRing R] [Field K]
    [Algebra A R] [Algebra A K] [IsFractionRing A K]
    (h : Function.Injective (algebraMap A R)) : Nontrivial (K ⊗[A] R) := by
  let : Algebra R (K ⊗[A] R) := Algebra.TensorProduct.rightAlgebra
  refine not_subsingleton_iff_nontrivial.mp fun hs => ?_
  obtain ⟨a, ha, heq⟩ :=
    (IsLocalization.subsingleton_iff (M := Algebra.algebraMapSubmonoid R A⁰)
      (S := K ⊗[A] R)).mp hs
  exact (nonZeroDivisors.ne_zero ha) (h (heq.trans (map_zero _).symm))

/-- **Regularity passes from a base change to the generic fibre.** If `A → R` is an injective map
of a domain `A` into a ring `R` and `C ⊗[A] R` is regular, then `C ⊗[A] K` is regular for `K` a
fraction field of `A`: inverting `A ∖ {0}` keeps `C ⊗[A] R` regular, and
`(K ⊗[A] C) ⊗[K] (K ⊗[A] R)` is faithfully flat over `K ⊗[A] C`. -/
theorem isRegularRing_tensorProduct_fractionRing_of_baseChange
    {A C R K : Type*} [CommRing A] [IsDomain A] [CommRing C] [CommRing R] [Field K]
    [Algebra A C] [Algebra A R] [Algebra A K] [IsFractionRing A K]
    [IsRegularRing (C ⊗[A] R)] (h : Function.Injective (algebraMap A R)) :
    IsRegularRing (C ⊗[A] K) := by
  let : Algebra (C ⊗[A] R) (K ⊗[A] (C ⊗[A] R)) := Algebra.TensorProduct.rightAlgebra
  have : IsRegularRing (K ⊗[A] (C ⊗[A] R)) :=
    isRegularRing_of_isLocalization
      (Algebra.algebraMapSubmonoid (C ⊗[A] R) A⁰)
  have : Nontrivial (K ⊗[A] R) := nontrivial_tensorProduct_fractionRing h
  let e : (K ⊗[A] C) ⊗[K] (K ⊗[A] R) ≃ₐ[K] K ⊗[A] (C ⊗[A] R) :=
    (Algebra.TensorProduct.cancelBaseChange A K K (K ⊗[A] C) R).trans
      (Algebra.TensorProduct.assoc A A K K C R)
  have : IsRegularRing ((K ⊗[A] C) ⊗[K] (K ⊗[A] R)) :=
    IsRegularRing.of_ringEquiv e.symm.toRingEquiv
  have : IsRegularRing (K ⊗[A] C) :=
    IsRegularRing.of_faithfullyFlat ((K ⊗[A] C) ⊗[K] (K ⊗[A] R))
  exact IsRegularRing.of_ringEquiv (Algebra.TensorProduct.comm A K C).toRingEquiv

/-- Normality of the `I`-adic completion of a finite algebra `D` from normality of the base
change `Rˆ ⊗[R] D`, the two being identified by `ofTensorProductAlgEquiv`. -/
private theorem isNormalRing_adicCompletion_of_tensorProduct
    (R : Type u) [CommRing R] [IsNoetherianRing R]
    (I : Ideal R) (D : Type u) [CommRing D] [Algebra R D] [Module.Finite R D]
    (h : IsNormalRing (AdicCompletion I R ⊗[R] D)) :
    IsNormalRing (AdicCompletion (I.map (algebraMap R D)) D) :=
  IsNormalRing.congr (ofTensorProductAlgEquiv I D).toRingEquiv h

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-! ### Geometric preliminaries -/

/-- Regularity of schemes transports along an isomorphism: the preimage of an affine open is an
affine open with isomorphic ring of sections. -/
theorem IsRegular.of_iso {X Y : Scheme.{u}} (e : X ≅ Y) (hY : IsRegular Y) :
    IsRegular X := by
  intro x
  obtain ⟨U, hxU, hreg⟩ := hY (e.hom.base x)
  have hrange : U.1 ≤ e.hom.opensRange := fun y _ => ⟨e.inv.base y, by simp⟩
  have : IsIso (e.hom.app U.1) := e.hom.isIso_app U.1 hrange
  exact ⟨⟨e.hom ⁻¹ᵁ U.1, U.2.preimage_of_isIso e.hom⟩, hxU,
    IsRegularRing.of_ringEquiv (asIso (e.hom.app U.1)).commRingCatIsoToRingEquiv⟩

/-- If `Spec S` is a regular scheme then `S` is a regular ring, `S` being the global sections. -/
private theorem isRegularRing_of_isRegular_spec (S : Type u) [CommRing S]
    (h : IsRegular (Spec (.of S))) : IsRegularRing S :=
  have : IsRegularRing Γ(Spec (.of S), ⊤) :=
    ((isRegular_tfae_cover (Spec (.of S))).out 1 2 rfl rfl).mp h ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩
  IsRegularRing.of_ringEquiv (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of S)).commRingCatIsoToRingEquiv

/-- On a locally Noetherian scheme every quasi-compact open has finitely many irreducible
components, being a Noetherian space. -/
@[ega "0 2.2.5" "special case", ega "I 7.3.3" "special case"]
private theorem finite_irreducibleComponents_of_isLocallyNoetherian {X : Scheme.{u}}
    (hX : IsLocallyNoetherian X) (U : X.Opens) (hU : IsCompact (U : Set X)) :
    (irreducibleComponents U).Finite := by
  have : CompactSpace U := isCompact_iff_compactSpace.mp hU
  have : NoetherianSpace U := noetherianSpace_of_isLocallyNoetherianSpace U
    (IsLocallyNoetherianSpace.subtype
      (isLocallyNoetherianSpace_of_isLocallyNoetherian X) U)
  exact NoetherianSpace.finite_irreducibleComponents

/-- **A regular open subscheme of `Spec A` contains a nonempty basic open.** If some open of
`Spec A` with a point is regular, then `A_a` is regular for some `a ≠ 0`. -/
theorem exists_isRegularRing_localizationAway_of_isRegular_opens
    (A : Type u) [CommRing A] [IsDomain A] (V : (Spec (.of A)).Opens)
    (hV : IsRegular V.toScheme) (x : V) :
    ∃ a : A, a ≠ 0 ∧ IsRegularRing (Localization.Away a) := by
  obtain ⟨_, ⟨a, rfl⟩, ha, hsub⟩ :=
    PrimeSpectrum.isTopologicalBasis_basic_opens.exists_subset_of_mem_open
      (show (x : Spec (.of A)) ∈ (V : Set (Spec (.of A))) from x.2) V.2
  have hane : a ≠ 0 := fun h => ha (h ▸ Ideal.zero_mem _)
  let d : Spec (.of (Localization.Away a)) ⟶ Spec (.of A) :=
    Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A (Localization.Away a)))
  have hd : Set.range d.base ⊆ Set.range V.ι.base := by
    rw [V.range_ι]
    exact le_trans (Scheme.Hom.opensRange_localizationAway (R := .of A) a).le hsub
  let l := IsOpenImmersion.lift V.ι d hd
  have hreg : IsRegular (Spec (.of (Localization.Away a))) :=
    IsRegular.of_iso (IsOpenImmersion.isoOfRangeEq l l.opensRange.ι (by simp))
      (hV.restrict l.opensRange)
  exact ⟨a, hane, isRegularRing_of_isRegular_spec _ hreg⟩

/-- A ring map from a domain whose induced map on spectra is dominant is injective: its kernel is
contained in the nilradical, which is zero. -/
private theorem injective_of_isDominant_specMap
    {A R : Type u} [CommRing A] [IsDomain A] [CommRing R]
    (φ : CommRingCat.of A ⟶ CommRingCat.of R) (h : IsDominant (Spec.map φ)) :
    Function.Injective φ.hom := by
  refine (RingHom.injective_iff_ker_eq_bot φ.hom).mpr (le_antisymm ?_ bot_le)
  simpa [nilradical_eq_zero] using
    (PrimeSpectrum.denseRange_comap_iff_ker_le_nilRadical φ.hom).mp h.denseRange

/-- For a dominant morphism from an integral quasi-compact scheme to an affine scheme, the map of
global sections is injective: its kernel is contained in the nilradical, which is zero. -/
private theorem globalSections_algebraMap_injective_of_isDominant
    (A : Type u) [CommRing A] [IsDomain A] (X : Scheme.{u}) [IsIntegral X]
    [CompactSpace X] (f : X ⟶ Spec (.of A)) (hf : IsDominant f) :
    Function.Injective (((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of A)).inv ≫ f.appTop).hom) := by
  let ψ := (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of A)).inv ≫ f.appTop
  have hcomp : X.toSpecΓ ≫ Spec.map ψ = f := by
    dsimp only [ψ]
    rw [Spec.map_comp]
    calc
      X.toSpecΓ ≫ Spec.map f.appTop ≫ Spec.map (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of A)).inv =
          (X.toSpecΓ ≫ Spec.map f.appTop) ≫ Spec.map (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of A)).inv := by
            simp [Category.assoc]
      _ = (f ≫ (Spec (.of A)).toSpecΓ) ≫ Spec.map (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of A)).inv := by
            rw [← Scheme.toSpecΓ_naturality f]
      _ = f := by simp
  have : IsDominant (X.toSpecΓ ≫ Spec.map ψ) := by rwa [hcomp]
  exact injective_of_isDominant_specMap ψ (IsDominant.of_comp X.toSpecΓ (Spec.map ψ))

/-- The global sections of a finite coproduct of normal integral schemes form a normal ring,
being the product of the rings of global sections of the parts. -/
private theorem isNormalRing_globalSections_of_iso_coproduct
    {X : Scheme.{u}} {ι : Type u} (Y : ι → Scheme.{u}) [Finite ι]
    (e : X ≅ ∐ Y) (hYnormal : ∀ i, IsNormal (Y i)) (hYintegral : ∀ i, IsIntegral (Y i)) :
    IsNormalRing Γ(X, ⊤) := by
  classical
  let hΓ : IsColimit (Cofan.mk (Scheme.Γ.rightOp.obj (∐ Y))
      (fun i => Scheme.Γ.rightOp.map (Sigma.ι Y i))) :=
    isColimitCofanMkObjOfIsColimit Scheme.Γ.rightOp Y (Sigma.ι Y) (coproductIsCoproduct Y)
  let cPi : Cofan (fun i => Scheme.Γ.rightOp.obj (Y i)) :=
    Cofan.mk (Opposite.op (CommRingCat.of (∀ i, Γ(Y i, ⊤))))
      (fun i => show Scheme.Γ.rightOp.obj (Y i) ⟶
          Opposite.op (CommRingCat.of (∀ i, Γ(Y i, ⊤))) from
        (CommRingCat.ofHom (Pi.evalRingHom (fun i => Γ(Y i, ⊤)) i)).op)
  let hPi : IsColimit cPi := by
    refine Cofan.IsColimit.mk cPi (fun t =>
      (CommRingCat.ofHom (RingHom.pi fun i => (t.inj i).unop.hom)).op) ?_ ?_
    · intro t i
      apply Quiver.Hom.unop_inj
      ext x
      rfl
    · intro t m hm
      apply Quiver.Hom.unop_inj
      ext x
      funext i
      exact DFunLike.congr_fun (congrArg CommRingCat.Hom.hom (congrArg Quiver.Hom.unop (hm i))) x
  have hSum : IsNormalRing Γ(∐ Y, ⊤) := by
    refine IsNormalRing.congr
      ((hΓ.coconePointUniqueUpToIso hPi).symm.unop).commRingCatIsoToRingEquiv.symm ?_
    refine isNormalRing_pi fun i => ?_
    have : IsIntegral (Y i) := hYintegral i
    have : IsNormal (Y i) := hYnormal i
    have : IsIntegrallyClosed Γ(Y i, ⊤) := normal_globalSections (Y i)
    exact IsNormalRing.of_isIntegrallyClosed Γ(Y i, ⊤)
  exact IsNormalRing.congr (Scheme.Γ.mapIso e.op).symm.commRingCatIsoToRingEquiv.symm hSum

/-- A coproduct of nonempty schemes which is quasi-compact has a finite index type. -/
private theorem finite_index_of_compactSpace_coproduct
    {ι : Type u} (Y : ι → Scheme.{u}) [CompactSpace (∐ Y : Scheme.{u})]
    (hY : ∀ i, Nonempty (Y i)) : Finite ι := by
  have : CompactSpace (Σ i, Y i) := (sigmaMk Y).symm.compactSpace
  obtain ⟨s, t, hs, _, heq⟩ :=
    (isCompact_univ : IsCompact (Set.univ : Set (Σ i, Y i))).sigma_exists_finite_sigma_eq Set.univ
  refine Set.finite_univ_iff.mp (hs.subset fun i _ => ?_)
  obtain ⟨y⟩ := hY i
  exact (show (⟨i, y⟩ : Σ i, Y i) ∈ s.sigma t from heq.symm ▸ Set.mem_univ _).1

/-- **The global sections of a quasi-compact normal locally Noetherian scheme form a normal
ring.** By [Stacks, Tag 0357] the scheme is a coproduct of normal integral schemes, and
quasi-compactness makes the coproduct finite. -/
private theorem isNormalRing_globalSections_of_isNormal
    {X : Scheme.{u}} [CompactSpace X] (hX : IsNormal X) (hN : IsLocallyNoetherian X) :
    IsNormalRing Γ(X, ⊤) := by
  obtain ⟨ι, Y, hYnormal, hYintegral, ⟨e⟩⟩ :=
    (isNormal_iff_exists_iso_coproduct
      (finite_irreducibleComponents_of_isLocallyNoetherian hN)).mp hX
  have : CompactSpace (∐ Y : Scheme.{u}) := e.hom.homeomorph.compactSpace
  have : Finite ι := finite_index_of_compactSpace_coproduct Y fun i => by
    have : IsIntegral (Y i) := hYintegral i
    infer_instance
  exact isNormalRing_globalSections_of_iso_coproduct Y e hYnormal hYintegral

/-- **Flat base change of the global sections of a proper regular scheme over an affine base.**
For `f : X ⟶ Spec A` proper with `X ×_{Spec A} Spec D` regular and `Spec D ⟶ Spec A` flat, the
ring `D ⊗[A] Γ(X, 𝒪_X)` is normal: it is the ring of global sections of the base change, which is
quasi-compact, normal and locally Noetherian. -/
private theorem isNormalRing_tensorProduct_globalSections_of_isRegular_pullback
    (A D : Type u) [CommRing A] [CommRing D] [Algebra A D]
    (X : Scheme.{u}) (f : X ⟶ Spec (.of A)) [IsProper f]
    [Flat (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A D)))]
    (h : IsRegular (pullback f (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A D))) : Scheme.{u})) :
    let : Algebra A Γ(X, ⊤) := ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of A)).inv ≫ f.appTop).hom.toAlgebra
    IsNormalRing (D ⊗[A] Γ(X, ⊤)) := by
  let : Algebra A Γ(X, ⊤) := ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of A)).inv ≫ f.appTop).hom.toAlgebra
  let g : Spec (.of D) ⟶ Spec (.of A) := Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A D))
  let Y : Scheme.{u} := pullback f g
  have : CompactSpace X := QuasiCompact.compactSpace_of_compactSpace f
  have : QuasiSeparatedSpace X := (quasiSeparated_iff_quasiSeparatedSpace f).mp inferInstance
  have : CompactSpace Y := QuasiCompact.compactSpace_of_compactSpace (pullback.snd f g)
  have hY : IsNormalRing Γ(Y, ⊤) :=
    isNormalRing_globalSections_of_isNormal (isNormal_of_isRegular Y h)
      (isLocallyNoetherian_of_isRegular h)
  have hpush₀ : IsPushout f.appTop g.appTop
      (pullback.fst f g).appTop (pullback.snd f g).appTop :=
    isPushout_appTop_of_flat (IsPullback.of_hasPullback f g)
  let α := Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of A)
  let β := Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of D)
  have hpush : IsPushout
      (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A Γ(X, ⊤)))
      (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A D))
      (pullback.fst f g).appTop
      (β.inv ≫ (pullback.snd f g).appTop) := by
    apply hpush₀.of_iso α (Iso.refl _) β (Iso.refl _)
    · simp [α, RingHom.algebraMap_toAlgebra]
    · simp [g, α, β]
    · simp
    · simp
  have htensor : IsNormalRing (Γ(X, ⊤) ⊗[A] D) :=
    IsNormalRing.congr
      ((CommRingCat.isPushout_tensorProduct A Γ(X, ⊤) D).isoIsPushout
        (.of Γ(X, ⊤)) (.of D) hpush).commRingCatIsoToRingEquiv.symm hY
  exact IsNormalRing.congr (Algebra.TensorProduct.comm A D Γ(X, ⊤)).toRingEquiv.symm htensor

/-- The global sections of a proper regular alteration of `Spec A` form an integrally closed
domain, finite over `A` by the degree-zero case of [Stacks, Tag 02O6], with `A` mapping into it
injectively. -/
private theorem globalSections_of_regular_alteration
    (A : Type u) [CommRing A] [IsDomain A] [IsNoetherianRing A]
    (X : Scheme.{u}) (f : X ⟶ Spec (.of A)) (hf : IsAlteration f) (hX : IsRegular X) :
    let : Algebra A Γ(X, ⊤) := ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of A)).inv ≫ f.appTop).hom.toAlgebra
    Module.Finite A Γ(X, ⊤) ∧ IsDomain Γ(X, ⊤) ∧ IsIntegrallyClosed Γ(X, ⊤) ∧
      Function.Injective (algebraMap A Γ(X, ⊤)) := by
  let : Algebra A Γ(X, ⊤) := ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of A)).inv ≫ f.appTop).hom.toAlgebra
  have : IsIntegral X := hf.2.2.1
  have : IsProper f := hf.1
  have : CompactSpace X := QuasiCompact.compactSpace_of_compactSpace f
  have : Nonempty (⊤ : X.Opens) := ⟨⟨Classical.choice (inferInstance : Nonempty X), trivial⟩⟩
  have : IsDomain Γ(X, ⊤) := IsIntegral.component_integral (⊤ : X.Opens)
  have : IsNormal X := isNormal_of_isRegular X hX
  refine ⟨module_finite_globalSections f (finiteGlobalSectionsOfProper A inferInstance f hf.1),
    inferInstance, normal_globalSections X, ?_⟩
  simpa [RingHom.algebraMap_toAlgebra] using
    globalSections_algebraMap_injective_of_isDominant A X f hf.2.1

/-! ### The implied properties -/

/-- **A Noetherian local domain admitting an alteration by a regular scheme is regular after
inverting one nonzero element.** This is part (1) of [Stacks, Tag 0BGI]: the dense regular open
of [Stacks, Tag 0BGG] contains a nonempty basic open `D(a)` of `Spec A`, and `Γ(D(a)) = A_a`. -/
@[stacks 0BGI "part (1)"]
theorem exists_isRegularRing_localizationAway_of_regular_alteration
    (A : Type u) [CommRing A] [IsDomain A] [IsNoetherianRing A] [IsLocalRing A]
    (X : Scheme.{u}) (f : X ⟶ Spec (.of A)) (hf : IsAlteration f) (hX : IsRegular X) :
    ∃ a : A, a ≠ 0 ∧ IsRegularRing (Localization.Away a) := by
  obtain ⟨V, hVdense, hVreg⟩ := exists_dense_open_isRegular (Spec (.of A)) X f hf hX
  obtain ⟨x, hx⟩ := hVdense.nonempty
  exact exists_isRegularRing_localizationAway_of_isRegular_opens A V hVreg ⟨x, hx⟩

/-- **The integral closure of a Noetherian local domain admitting an alteration by a regular
scheme is a finite module over it.** This is part (2) of [Stacks, Tag 0BGI]: the global sections
`C` of the regular alteration are a finite `A`-module — by the degree-zero case of
[Stacks, Tag 02O6], `AlgebraicGeometry.finiteGlobalSectionsOfProper` — and an integrally closed
domain containing `A`, so the integral closure of `A` in `Frac(A)` embeds into `C` and is a
submodule of a finite module over the Noetherian ring `A`. -/
@[stacks 0BGI "part (2)"]
theorem module_finite_integralClosure_of_regular_alteration
    (A : Type u) [CommRing A] [IsDomain A] [IsNoetherianRing A] [IsLocalRing A]
    (X : Scheme.{u}) (f : X ⟶ Spec (.of A)) (hf : IsAlteration f) (hX : IsRegular X) :
    Module.Finite A ↥(integralClosure A (FractionRing A)) := by
  let : Algebra A Γ(X, ⊤) := ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of A)).inv ≫ f.appTop).hom.toAlgebra
  obtain ⟨hfin, hdom, hclosed, hinj⟩ := globalSections_of_regular_alteration A X f hf hX
  have := hfin
  have := hdom
  have := hclosed
  exact Module.Finite.of_injective
    (integralClosureToIntegrallyClosed (K := FractionRing A) hinj).toLinearMap
    (integralClosureToIntegrallyClosed_injective hinj)

/-- **The completion of the integral closure is normal.** This is part (3) of
[Stacks, Tag 0BGI]. With `C = Γ(X, 𝒪_X)` and `B` the integral closure of `A` in `Frac(A)`, the
inclusion `B ⊆ C` is a map of finite `A`-algebras, `B` is a normal domain, and the completion of
`C` is normal because the base change of `X` to `Spec Aˆ` stays regular ([Stacks, Tag 0BG6]) and
its global sections are `Aˆ ⊗_A C` ([Stacks, Tag 02KH]); [Stacks, Tag 0BGH] then gives normality
of `Bˆ`. -/
@[stacks 0BGI "part (3)"]
theorem isNormalRing_adicCompletion_integralClosure_of_regular_alteration
    (A : Type u) [CommRing A] [IsDomain A] [IsNoetherianRing A] [IsLocalRing A]
    (X : Scheme.{u}) (f : X ⟶ Spec (.of A)) (hf : IsAlteration f) (hX : IsRegular X) :
    IsNormalRing
      (AdicCompletion
        ((IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A).map
          (algebraMap A ↥(integralClosure A (FractionRing A))))
        ↥(integralClosure A (FractionRing A))) := by
  let : Algebra A Γ(X, ⊤) := ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of A)).inv ≫ f.appTop).hom.toAlgebra
  have : IsProper f := hf.1
  obtain ⟨hfin, hdom, hclosed, hinj⟩ := globalSections_of_regular_alteration A X f hf hX
  have := hfin
  have := hdom
  have := hclosed
  -- The integral closure is a normal domain, and maps injectively into `Γ(X, ⊤)`.
  have : IsNormalDomain ↥(integralClosure A (FractionRing A)) :=
    integralClosure_isNormalDomain (R := A) (S := FractionRing A) ⟨inferInstance, inferInstance⟩
  let φ : ↥(integralClosure A (FractionRing A)) →ₐ[A] Γ(X, ⊤) :=
    integralClosureToIntegrallyClosed (K := FractionRing A) hinj
  let : Algebra ↥(integralClosure A (FractionRing A)) Γ(X, ⊤) := φ.toAlgebra
  have : IsScalarTower A ↥(integralClosure A (FractionRing A)) Γ(X, ⊤) :=
    IsScalarTower.of_algebraMap_eq' φ.comp_algebraMap.symm
  have : Module.Finite A ↥(integralClosure A (FractionRing A)) :=
    module_finite_integralClosure_of_regular_alteration A X f hf hX
  -- The completion of `Γ(X, ⊤)` is normal, by regularity of the base change to `Spec Aˆ`.
  have : Flat (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom
      (algebraMap A (AdicCompletion (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A) A)))) :=
    Flat.SpecMap_iff.mpr (RingHom.flat_algebraMap_iff.mpr inferInstance)
  have hCD : IsNormalRing
      (TensorProduct A (AdicCompletion (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A) A) Γ(X, ⊤)) :=
    isNormalRing_tensorProduct_globalSections_of_isRegular_pullback A
      (AdicCompletion (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A) A) X f
      ((isRegular_pullback_completion_iff A X f).mp hX)
  exact isNormalRing_adicCompletion_of_finite_injective A
    ↥(integralClosure A (FractionRing A)) Γ(X, ⊤)
    (integralClosureToIntegrallyClosed_injective hinj) (IsNormalRing.of_isIntegrallyClosed _)
    (isNormalRing_adicCompletion_of_tensorProduct A (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A) Γ(X, ⊤) hCD)

/-- **The generic formal fibre of a Noetherian local domain admitting an alteration by a regular
scheme is regular.** This is part (4) of [Stacks, Tag 0BGI]. Taking an affine open `U ⊆ X` around
the generic point and `R = Γ(X, U)`, the scheme `Spec (R ⊗_A Aˆ)` is an open subscheme of the
regular `X ×_{Spec A} Spec Aˆ` ([Stacks, Tag 0BG6]), so `Aˆ ⊗_A R` is regular; the generic formal
fibre is recovered by inverting `A ∖ {0}` and descending along the faithfully flat
`Frac(A)`-algebra `Frac(A) ⊗_A R`. -/
@[stacks 0BGI "part (4)", ega "IV 7.9.3" "domain case"]
theorem isRegularRing_genericFormalFibre_of_regular_alteration
    (A : Type u) [CommRing A] [IsDomain A] [IsNoetherianRing A] [IsLocalRing A]
    (X : Scheme.{u}) (f : X ⟶ Spec (.of A)) (hf : IsAlteration f) (hX : IsRegular X) :
    IsRegularRing ((AdicCompletion (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A) A) ⊗[A] (FractionRing A)) := by
  let C := AdicCompletion (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A) A
  have : IsIntegral X := hf.2.2.1
  have : IsProper f := hf.1
  -- An affine open `U` of `X` around the generic point, with `R = Γ(X, U)`.
  obtain ⟨_, ⟨W, hW, rfl⟩, hηW, _⟩ :=
    X.isBasis_affineOpens.exists_subset_of_mem_open (Set.mem_univ (genericPoint X)) isOpen_univ
  let U : X.affineOpens := ⟨W, hW⟩
  let R := Γ(X, U.1)
  let v : (U.1).toScheme ⟶ X := U.1.ι
  let q : Spec (.of R) ⟶ Spec (.of A) := U.2.isoSpec.symm.hom ≫ v ≫ f
  obtain ⟨φ, hφ⟩ := Spec.map_surjective q
  let : Algebra A R := φ.hom.toAlgebra
  -- `A → R` is injective, `U` being dense in `X` and `f` dominant.
  have hq : IsDominant q := by
    have : IsDominant v := Opens.isDominant_ι
      ((dense_iff_closure_eq.mpr (genericPoint_spec X).def).mono
        (Set.singleton_subset_iff.mpr hηW))
    have : IsDominant f := hf.2.1
    infer_instance
  have hφinj : Function.Injective (algebraMap A R) :=
    injective_of_isDominant_specMap φ (hφ ▸ hq)
  -- `R ⊗[A] Aˆ` is regular, being an open subscheme of the regular `X ×_{Spec A} Spec Aˆ`.
  let g : Spec (.of C) ⟶ Spec (.of A) := Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A C))
  have hXhat : IsRegular (pullback f g : Scheme.{u}) :=
    (isRegular_pullback_completion_iff A X f).mp hX
  let w : Spec (.of R) ⟶ X := U.2.isoSpec.symm.hom ≫ v
  have : IsOpenImmersion w := inferInstance
  have hV : IsRegular (pullback w (pullback.fst f g) : Scheme.{u}) :=
    IsRegular.of_iso
      (IsOpenImmersion.isoOfRangeEq (pullback.snd w (pullback.fst f g))
        (pullback.snd w (pullback.fst f g)).opensRange.ι (by simp))
      (hXhat.restrict (pullback.snd w (pullback.fst f g)).opensRange)
  have hQ : IsRegular (pullback q g : Scheme.{u}) :=
    IsRegular.of_iso (pullbackRightPullbackFstIso f g w).symm hV
  have hTensorSpec : IsRegular (Spec (.of (R ⊗[A] C))) :=
    IsRegular.of_iso
      ((pullback.congrHom hφ.symm rfl) ≪≫ pullbackSpecIso A R C).symm hQ
  have : IsRegularRing (R ⊗[A] C) := isRegularRing_of_isRegular_spec _ hTensorSpec
  have : IsRegularRing (C ⊗[A] R) :=
    IsRegularRing.of_ringEquiv (Algebra.TensorProduct.comm A R C).toRingEquiv
  exact isRegularRing_tensorProduct_fractionRing_of_baseChange
    (C := C) (R := R) (K := FractionRing A) hφinj

end AlgebraicGeometry

